A||||1||Thor||Tail light wire harness for 86GT problem||||1||
Z||000000||Thor||08-27-2000||10:34 PM||||OK All I want to do is repair a license plate bulb socket wire and noticed the main harness is not visable when you remove the tail lens assembly...My God am I going to have to remove the rear facia and perhaps the bumper/honeycomb to get to this harness? I also want to inspect the harness for other candadates leading to my parking light problem[20amp fuse blows when actuated]. Thank you all in advance...I really want to get this problem solved It's been a long time since I'v been able to leagaly drive at night !||||reg||1
Z||000001||007DOUG||08-28-2000||01:11 AM||||YEP, and remember to smile while you're doing it.<P>Remove the taillights, and then remove the plastic pop rivots along the top of the facia. The bumper is flexable enough to reach the wiring. The honeycomb can stay.<P>Depending on how far you need to go with the wiring, you may need to remove the metal support bar that those rivots fastened into. You'll find 10mm bolts under that bar.<P>But to remove this bar, you'll have to remove the screws found under the side markerlights, and remove the screws along the inner fenders. This will allow the facia to swing down and out of your way.  ||||reg||13
